$DIR/main.p:22:15: cannot store readAll(1).Ptr() in package variable keep, which outlives the temporary
    readAll(1).Ptr() points into the temporary Buf that readAll(1) returns. The
    Buf that readAll(1) returns (at main.p:22) is a temporary: nothing keeps it,
    so it is the receiver of the method only until the end of the statement. A
    view of it may be passed to calls in that statement but may not outlive it.
    At the end of the statement, the temporary is dropped, but package variable
    keep lives longer, so it would be left pointing at a value that has been
    dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Keep the owner in a variable, so that it lives until the end of its scope,
    and call the method on the variable:
        v := readAll(1)
        ... v.Ptr() ...
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
